% Every goal delivered: after a goal is given, its result is delivered, as done or as
% failed, on every way the run can go on. Along the way every run keeps going until it
% ends (see no-deadlock), so this holds without a fairness assumption when the
% environment answers each task it was given and does nothing else; an environment that
% may stop answering would need the assumption that it does not.
forall t: Task . [true* . goal(t)] mu Y . ([!(exists b: Bool . deliver(t, b))] Y && <true> true)
